            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 1</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"img4\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('img4', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Sacred mountain at Xunantunich, Belize. Photograph taken on <htdate0>, during a visit to the site.</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Equal, same group, or different? - A game to reinforce comparisons: things can be equal, belong to the same group, or be completely different. (<htcite0>)</li><li>Naming - After seeing how we can fill in values between numbers, how about we name them? (<htcite1>)</li><li>Together we are strong - In this text, we see how the four operations, when combined, open the doors to so much knowledge (<htcite2>)</li><li>Classifying equality - In this text, we see that classifying is more than comparing things that are exactly alike. (<htcite3>)</li><li>The result is (Phase II) - a game to reinforce the connection between addition and multiplication. (<htcite4>)</li><li>Translation game (Part I) - Explore numbers from different cultures through an engaging translation game. (<htcite5>)</li><li>The result is - a game of consecutive sums that helps uncover the story. (<htcite6>)</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
